// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; T27 OS glass window -- the 27-petal home as a native macOS window, written in t27 and built by t27b.
; No HTML, no Swift: t27b compiles this module to an arm64 Mach-O object (`t27b build --macho`), and
; `ld` links it against AppKit, CoreGraphics, CoreText and libobjc. Every call into the system goes
; through an import, `fn f(..) T { return @extern("sym"); }` (t27b extern boundary, #8946).
//
; It behaves as the trios app does (BrowserOS/trios TriosTabView + QueenUI MainView, read 2026-10-19):
;   W  window   -- NSWindow 960 x 540 pt, transparent title bar, content = NSVisualEffectView, dark
;                  appearance, behind-window blending, black tint 0.30 (trios blackGlass nativeTint).
;                  The frame itself is clear in a window -- matte black glass, as in trios (owner,
;                  2026-10-20, superseding the 2026-10-19 opaque black for a window). Full screen has no
;                  transparency, so there the layer and the frame are opaque black #000000.
;   T  title    -- trios title bar, 34 pt: the logo 17 x 14 (petal_menu style, 0.5 pt outline) + "TRINITY" = home,
;                  centred in the bar as one group (owner, 2026-10-19), fullscreen control on the right,
;                  1 pt white 0.14 divider under it. The back chevron stays left, right of the traffic lights.
;   H  home     -- the logo alone, centred in the area under the title bar at 0.63 of its height (0.8 of that in full screen), in
;                  petal_menu's style (idle black 0.22, hover white, 1 px white outline), flying in as
;                  petal_glass.t27 does. Hovering a petal shows the trios tooltip: a white 0.94 pill,
;                  corner 6, 30 pt above the petal centre, "NAME  Cmd+1" in black semibold mono 13.
;   S  screen   -- a petal tap (or Cmd/Option/Control + 1..9, as QueenMenuShortcutPolicy) swaps the
;                  home for a full-area screen with an opacity cross-fade of 0.25 s (8 frames). There is
;                  one bar: the title bar gains the back chevron before the logo (click, Escape or
;                  Cmd+0 = home) and the refresh arc left of the dock control; no second header.
;   C  chat     -- the screen is trios' expanded chat workspace: a 272 pt sidebar (black 0.22) with the
;                  AGENTS label and the queen row (white crown, no other hue); tapping a cell opens that agent's
;                  chat, "+" at the right of the header opens one more (several chats per agent), and the x
;                  on a hovered AGENTS row closes that chat; "+" in the SPACES label opens a space, the x on a
;                  hovered space row closes it with its chats; the foot reads OPEN SOURCE T27 and opens
;                  the repository,
;                  a white 0.14 x 0.7 divider, then the content (black 0.14) with a 44 pt header -- the
;                  sidebar toggle (28 x 28, or Cmd+Shift+S; collapses at once, no animation) and the
;                  title -- and the 3 x 3 card slots in a readable column of at most 900 pt.
;   K  compact  -- trios WindowManager + ChatWorkspaceLayout: the sidebar.right control left of fullscreen docks
;                  the window as the 400 pt panel on the right edge, full visible height (animated; again
;                  = restore). Below 760 pt the workspace is compact: no sidebar, an "OPEN DASHBOARD" bar
;                  (elevated 0.25, 1 pt border 0.3) over the cards; tapping it forces the dashboard, whose
;                  header gains "Close Dashboard" (rectangle.compress.vertical) right of the toggle. The
;                  narrow scene is the view point for point, the logo fits its width. (Letter tracking 0.5
;                  of the bar text and the empty queen supervisor bar are not drawn.)
;   Q  queen    -- Cmd+J or the QUEEN row opens her panel over any view (queen.t27): what the user is
;                  looking at, the last eight controls pressed, one suggestion behind Confirm / Dismiss,
;                  and GOD MODE (box filled = on): with the panel open and the user still 3 s she runs the
;                  suggestion herself and logs it; Cmd+J, Escape, the box or closing the panel stops it.
;   T  term     -- a Claude Code chat shows a live terminal pane (term_pane.t27, vt.t27): the agent runs
;                  in the PTY server (pty_server.t27) reached over ~/.t27os/pty.sock, so it outlives the
;                  window; reopening the window re-finds the same pane. No server: offline, keys echo.
;   E  editor   -- T27 OS opens inside (owner, 2026-10-20): KEYS > OPEN IN leads with a "T27 OS" chip that
;                  runs a terminal editor (vim, nvim, hx, micro, nano; editors.t27) on the space's folder in
;                  a pane of the PTY server and shows it in the same terminal area in place of the chat's
;                  pane. Escape twice, the chip again, or another chat or space brings the chat back; the
;                  editor keeps running in the server.
;   D  dock     -- app icon: the logo white on a black squircle, drawn at launch.
; Not drawn (no server behind them yet): the Online dot, search, swarm and
; history lists, Cmd+K / Cmd+/ overlays, the formula in the tooltip. The Queen has no model
; behind her yet: her suggestion is a fixed rule over the sidebar.
; CoreGraphics rasterises (anti-aliased paths, CoreText lines) into a 4x bitmap that becomes the
; layer's contents. Epic gHashTag/t27#10782.

